// The HP pools of the boxes that carry one: the one crew pool every crew station of every tank
// shares, and the sturdiness classes every other box's pool is authored from, in HP points per m²
// of the box's mean face. Read by `src/ballistics/box_classes.rs`, embedded and parsed once,
// validated at parse.
//
// A crew station's pool is `crew_hp`, filled in when a tank file is parsed; a tank file that
// authors `hp` on a crew-facet volume does not load (`src/spec.rs`). Every other pool (`hp` in
// `<tank>.tank.ron`'s `volumes`) is authored as its class × the box's measured mean face, the
// mean of the three axis-aligned face areas of its bounds in the tank's sim geometry, rounded to a
// whole point; `src/tests/box_pools.rs` holds every tank asset to within ±25 % of that, and every
// crew pool to `crew_hp`. The class follows the box's facets: an ammunition box is `ammo`, any
// other box with a pool `hard`. So a box of one class at one place in the field fares as any other
// box of that class there, whatever its size: the field's dose to a box grows with the face it
// presents, and so does its pool. The law is design doc §6,
// `.agents/docs/design/armor-penetration-and-damage.md`; the decision is #3 in
// `.agents/scratch/damage-cam-2026-10-08/research/ap-aphe-2026-10-23/decision-2026-10-23.md`.
//
// PROVENANCE: every value is authored `(value, Kind("source or reason"))`, Kind one of Measured,
// Derived, Tuned, Resolution, Unknown (`src/provenance.rs`); a value without one does not load.
(
    crew_hp: (30, Tuned("owner decision 2026-10-23, provisional: one pool for every crew station
        of every tank, revised if play shows it out of proportion to the tank's other pools. A
        crewman is one entity across tanks, and the crew box is a placeholder for a humanoid
        shape, so its face is no basis for a pool. The field's calibration in spall_cone.ron and
        the crew line rate in rounds.ron are set against it")),
    ammo: (150, Tuned("as fragile per m² as the crew pool at the intended humanoid's 0.2 m² face
        (DERIVED: 30 / 0.2): a propellant case a fragment reaches is lost. The hard class would
        leave a bin a round's line passes straight through in action (pen cam scenario s5)")),
    hard: (300, Tuned("owner decision 2026-10-23: sturdier components hold up a little better,
        never through half a cone; twice the ammo class per m²")),
)
